<% content_for(:title, "About — Solana Bytes") %>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <div class="text-center mb-10">
    <%= pixel_logo(variant: :dark, size: 64, css_class: "mx-auto mb-5") %>
    <h1 class="text-white mb-2" style="font-size:24px;text-shadow:4px 4px 0 #4c1d95">About</h1>
    <p class="text-purple-300" style="font-size:13px">
      A field guide to Solana accounts.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# What %>
  <section class="pixel-card mb-6" style="padding:24px">
    <h2 class="text-white mb-3" style="font-size:14px;text-shadow:2px 2px 0 #4c1d95">
      What it is
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-3" style="font-size:11px;line-height:1.9">
      Solana Bytes is an interactive hex visualizer for Solana accounts paired
      with a Byte Challenge game.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-400" style="font-size:11px;line-height:1.9">
      Paste any account address to see decoded metadata and raw bytes with
      hover tooltips for every field. Play the Challenge to test your knowledge
      of Solana data structures &mdash; find specific fields in hex dumps, build
      streaks, climb the leaderboard.
    </p>
  </section>

  <%# Why %>
  <section class="pixel-card mb-6" style="padding:24px">
    <h2 class="text-white mb-3" style="font-size:14px;text-shadow:2px 2px 0 #4c1d95">
      Why it exists
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-3" style="font-size:11px;line-height:1.9">
      Solana&rsquo;s existing explorers are great for transactions but
      treat raw account data as an opaque blob. If you want to understand
      what a Stake account, a Vote account, or a Metaplex Metadata account
      actually <em>is</em> at the byte level, you read the source.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-400" style="font-size:11px;line-height:1.9">
      Solana Bytes is the byte-level guide that we wanted when we were learning
      &mdash; one place to inspect, decode, and practice on the layouts that
      every Solana developer eventually touches.
    </p>
  </section>

  <%# Who %>
  <section class="pixel-card mb-6" style="padding:24px">
    <h2 class="text-white mb-3" style="font-size:14px;text-shadow:2px 2px 0 #4c1d95">
      Who built it
    </h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-3" style="font-size:11px;line-height:1.9">
      Built for the <strong class="text-purple-300">Colosseum Frontier Hackathon</strong>
      by the team behind <a href="https://solrengine.org" class="text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SolRengine</a>
      &mdash; an open-source Rails engine for Solana wallet auth, RPC, and account decoding.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-400" style="font-size:11px;line-height:1.9">
      Solana Bytes is the reference application that demonstrates the engine
      end-to-end: wallet sign-in, RPC fetching with retry, per-program account
      decoding, and a real game loop on top.
    </p>
  </section>

  <%# Tech stack %>
  <section class="pixel-card mb-6" style="padding:24px">
    <h2 class="text-white mb-3" style="font-size:14px;text-shadow:2px 2px 0 #4c1d95">
      Tech stack
    </h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300" style="font-size:10px;line-height:1.8">
      <li><span class="text-purple-300">Rails 8.1</span> &middot; Hotwire (Turbo + Stimulus) &middot; Tailwind v4</li>
      <li><span class="text-purple-300">SolRengine</span> &middot; wallet auth (SIWS) + RPC client + account decoders</li>
      <li><span class="text-purple-300">SQLite</span> + Solid Queue / Cache / Cable</li>
      <li><span class="text-purple-300">Press Start 2P</span> font &middot; inline SVG pixel sprites &middot; pixel-art everywhere</li>
      <li><span class="text-purple-300">Fly.io</span> for hosting &middot; Kamal for deploys</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <%# Links %>
  <section class="pixel-card" style="padding:24px">
    <h2 class="text-white mb-3" style="font-size:14px;text-shadow:2px 2px 0 #4c1d95">
      Links
    </h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <a href="https://github.com/solrengine/solana-bytes" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
         class="text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300 inline-flex items-center gap-2" style="font-size:11px">
        <%= pixel_icon(:github, size: 14) %>
        GitHub repo
      </a>
      <a href="https://solrengine.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
         class="text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300" style="font-size:11px">
        SolRengine
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
